  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Stationary ball-handling countdown",
  "description": "Every player has a ball and spreads out so nobody can reach anyone else, facing the coach. The coach picks a move – for example crossover, between the legs or behind the back – and counts down: first two regular dribbles between each move, then one dribble, then no dribbles at all so the moves run together. The coach changes step every five to ten seconds and then changes the move, without stopping. Go non-stop for two to three minutes.\n\nWorks on the sideline or in a hallway before practice, and with any number of players. If there is room, players can walk slowly forward instead of standing still; beginners start stationary.\n\nVariations: count the other way (no dribbles first, then one, then two), start from three dribbles, or do doubles (two crossovers in a row and so on).",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pound the ball hard into the floor – it builds quicker hands and better control."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Eyes up on the coach, not on the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Low, quick switches in front, between the legs and behind the back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you never lose the ball you are going too slowly – speed it up."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 1,
